  "body": "Slice 3 of #1440: the Fixtures page follows the WCS page's layout. Layout only: no command, parameter or project-file change; every edit and add still goes through its existing command. Fork synced at the current upstream main; branched from `upstream/main`, not stacked (see Overlap).\n\nWhat changed\n- New `fixtures_page.rs` (the page, moved out of `pages.rs`, which is far past the 400-line law; `pages.rs` re-exports `fixtures_section`, so the dozen tests that draw it are untouched).\n- Two titled groups: \"Workholding\" (the quiet state line, each fixture's row, the machine-table line) and \"Add workholding\".\n- The four adds are `wcs_page::even_row` equal full-width buttons, one to a row (two to a row clipped \"Add built-in vise...\" and \"Add fixture plate...\" at the default pane width). \"Mark X as fixture\" stays conditional (exactly one model selected) on its own row under them, so nothing above it jumps.\n- A separator divides one fixture's row from the next. `fixture_rows` itself is not reshaped (own pane-fit pins from #509; its own slice if wanted) - see `docs/decisions/1440-fixtures-page-tidy.md`.\n- #1432's `labelled_by` names are untouched.\n\nOverlap\n- #1438 (browser file buttons) changes the \"Import fixture...\" button in `fixtures_section` to `browser_files::button` (greyed with a reason in the browser build). This PR moves that function, so the two conflict textually in `pages.rs`; whichever merges second ports that one call into `fixtures_page.rs` (a greyed button can sit in `add_enabled_ui(.., even_row(..))`). #1209 / #1124 conflict with main already and are neighbouring hunks. #1460 (Stock) and #1465 (Tool list) merge cleanly with this branch (trial merge).\n\nTested (all in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/fixtures_page.rs`, structural, no PNG changed)\n- `the_fixtures_page_is_laid_out_in_groups_like_the_wcs_page`: group order, every row control (name, Place, Locate part, Unmark, Delete, Place on plate, Fixed, the vise row) inside Workholding, the four adds equal, one per row, one left edge, under their title.\n- `the_fixtures_page_keeps_its_empty_message_with_no_fixtures`: the empty state - the message sits in Workholding, the other state line is absent, all four adds and the page heading show, no Mark button.\n- `the_fixtures_page_keeps_the_machine_table_line`: with a machine that states its travel, the table line sits in Workholding after the last row.\n- `the_fixtures_page_adds_open_their_dialogs`: vise, accessory and plate buttons each open their own dialog.\n- `the_fixtures_page_offers_mark_for_exactly_one_selected_model`: Mark appears under the adds, same width, and tags the model.\n- `the_fixtures_page_keeps_every_input_named`: with the Place and Place-on-plate forms open, every input still has its accessible name (#1432).\n- Mutation checks (each turned a pin red, then restored): drop either group title (3 tests red); rename the Accessory button (3); replace the Import button (4); unequal button widths (2); change the empty message (1); change the full-state line (2); rename the machine-table line (1); never offer Mark (1); vise button queues the plate dialog (1); drop the fixture rows (2); strip `labelled_by` from the plate rows (the names test red - the single-site strip on a dowel field was not reached by the pin, the full strip was).\n- Gates: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green; ui lib single-threaded 680 passed; clippy ui and app `-D warnings` clean.\n- Not exercised: clicking \"Import fixture...\" (it opens a native file dialog; its place is pinned, its command is unchanged), and a real narrow window by hand.\n\nScreenshots: before/after attached below\n\nChangelog: Fixtures page: titled groups and the add buttons as equal full-width rows (#1440, PR #1471)\n\nRefs #1440\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
